{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-s5-equivariant-torus-knots","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:s5-equivariant-torus-knots","kind":"proposition","title":"$S_5$-equivariant torus-knot embeddings: only $T_{2,3}$ and $T_{2,5}$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-brings-surface"],"tags":["torus-knot","symmetry","s5","equivariant","leptons"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.TorusKnot.s5_equivariant_classification","text":"s5-equivariant-torus-knots.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/s5-equivariant-torus-knots.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:s5-equivariant-torus-knots\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Sigma</code> be a Riemann surface with automorphism group <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Aut}(\\Sigma) = S_5</code> (<a href=\"#def:brings-surface\">Bring's surface</a>). A torus knot <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{2, s}</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">s \\geq 3</code> coprime to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code> admits an equivariant embedding into <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Sigma</code> if and only if</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  s  \\in  \\{3,\\, 5\\}.</code></pre>\n<p><em>An equivariant embedding preserves the intrinsic cyclic symmetry <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Z}_s</code> of the knot.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/s5-equivariant-torus-knots.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Proposition","number":"16.2.3"}
